{"id":"3af2451590e4ff1d","group":"68","path":"68/68-df-inessential-expansion.md","title":"Expansions by Constants","display":"df-inessential-expansion — Expansions by Constants","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Recursion Theory (Shoenfield)","book_abbrev":"68","label":"68-df-inessential-expansion","aliases":["68-df-inessential-expansion"],"display":"df-inessential-expansion — Expansions by Constants","depends_on":["[[68-df-first-order-semantics]]"],"source_edition":"1993 original; 2016 Cambridge reissue, supplied PDF","source_location":"§11 p.35 / PDF 44, expansion and inessential expansion definitions","verification_status":"source-adapted-definition","source_proof_status":"definition-construction-reviewed"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Recursion Theory (Shoenfield)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"68"},{"key":"label","html":"68-df-inessential-expansion"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>68-df-inessential-expansion</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-inessential-expansion — Expansions by Constants"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"285deaa50ea04329\" href=\"?note=285deaa50ea04329\" title=\"68-df-first-order-semantics\">68-df-first-order-semantics</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_edition","html":"1993 original; 2016 Cambridge reissue, supplied PDF"},{"key":"source_location","html":"§11 p.35 / PDF 44, expansion and inessential expansion definitions"},{"key":"verification_status","html":"source-adapted-definition"},{"key":"source_proof_status","html":"definition-construction-reviewed"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\sigma=(I,J,\\alpha,\\beta)\">\\(\\sigma=(I,J,\\alpha,\\beta)\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\sigma&#39;=(I&#39;,J&#39;,\\alpha&#39;,\\beta&#39;)\">\\(\\sigma&#39;=(I&#39;,J&#39;,\\alpha&#39;,\\beta&#39;)\\)</span> 均为有限签名，解释接口见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"285deaa50ea04329\" href=\"?note=285deaa50ea04329\" title=\"68-df-first-order-semantics\">68-df-first-order-semantics</a>。<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M,M&#39;\">\\(M,M&#39;\\)</span> 是候选结构。原书零元函数符号就是常元；在下式中用 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\beta&#39;(j)=0\">\\(\\beta&#39;(j)=0\\)</span> 表示新符号是常元。</p>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Expansion}_{68}(M,\\sigma,M&#39;,\\sigma&#39;)\\;\\Longleftrightarrow\\;\\exists D,\\rho,\\phi,\\rho&#39;,\\phi&#39;\\;\\left(\\begin{aligned}&amp;\\operatorname{FOStr}_{68}(M,\\sigma)\\land\\operatorname{FOStr}_{68}(M&#39;,\\sigma&#39;)\\\\&amp;\\land M=(\\sigma,D,\\rho,\\phi)\\land M&#39;=(\\sigma&#39;,D,\\rho&#39;,\\phi&#39;)\\\\&amp;\\land I\\subseteq I&#39;\\land J\\subseteq J&#39;\\land\\alpha&#39;\\restriction I=\\alpha\\land\\beta&#39;\\restriction J=\\beta\\\\&amp;\\land\\rho&#39;\\restriction I=\\rho\\land\\phi&#39;\\restriction J=\\phi\\end{aligned}\\right).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\operatorname{Expansion}_{68}(M,\\sigma,M&#39;,\\sigma&#39;)\\;\\Longleftrightarrow\\;\\exists D,\\rho,\\phi,\\rho&#39;,\\phi&#39;\\;\\left(\\begin{aligned}&amp;\\operatorname{FOStr}_{68}(M,\\sigma)\\land\\operatorname{FOStr}_{68}(M&#39;,\\sigma&#39;)\\\\&amp;\\land M=(\\sigma,D,\\rho,\\phi)\\land M&#39;=(\\sigma&#39;,D,\\rho&#39;,\\phi&#39;)\\\\&amp;\\land I\\subseteq I&#39;\\land J\\subseteq J&#39;\\land\\alpha&#39;\\restriction I=\\alpha\\land\\beta&#39;\\restriction J=\\beta\\\\&amp;\\land\\rho&#39;\\restriction I=\\rho\\land\\phi&#39;\\restriction J=\\phi\\end{aligned}\\right).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{InessExp}_{68}(M,\\sigma,M&#39;,\\sigma&#39;)\\;\\Longleftrightarrow\\;\\operatorname{Expansion}_{68}(M,\\sigma,M&#39;,\\sigma&#39;)\\land I&#39;=I\\land\\forall j\\in J&#39;\\setminus J\\;\\beta&#39;(j)=0.\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\operatorname{InessExp}_{68}(M,\\sigma,M&#39;,\\sigma&#39;)\\;\\Longleftrightarrow\\;\\operatorname{Expansion}_{68}(M,\\sigma,M&#39;,\\sigma&#39;)\\land I&#39;=I\\land\\forall j\\in J&#39;\\setminus J\\;\\beta&#39;(j)=0.\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>原书 §11，印刷 p.35 / PDF p.44，在相同载体上保持旧符号解释，并只添加常元时称 inessential expansion。此处把相同载体、符号包含、元数一致与解释限制逐项写出；不把仅有同构而载体不同的结构误认作扩张。由于签名有限，新增常元也是有限个。编码语法按符号数值标识构造，所以旧语言公式可直接视为新语言的同一码。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"68-df-first-order-semantics","status":"resolved","id":"285deaa50ea04329","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[68-df-first-order-semantics]]","embed":false},{"target":"68-df-first-order-semantics","status":"resolved","id":"285deaa50ea04329","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\sigma=(I,J,\\alpha,\\beta)$，$\\sigma'=(I',J',\\alpha',\\beta')$ 均为有限签名，解释接口见 [[68-df-first-order-semantics]]。$M,M'$ 是候选结构。原书零元函数符号就是常元；在下式中用 $\\beta'(j)=0$ 表示新符号是常元。","embed":false}],"attachments":[],"math":[{"tex":"\\sigma=(I,J,\\alpha,\\beta)","display":false},{"tex":"\\sigma'=(I',J',\\alpha',\\beta')","display":false},{"tex":"M,M'","display":false},{"tex":"\\beta'(j)=0","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Expansion}_{68}(M,\\sigma,M',\\sigma')\\;\\Longleftrightarrow\\;\\exists D,\\rho,\\phi,\\rho',\\phi'\\;\\left(\\begin{aligned}&\\operatorname{FOStr}_{68}(M,\\sigma)\\land\\operatorname{FOStr}_{68}(M',\\sigma')\\\\&\\land M=(\\sigma,D,\\rho,\\phi)\\land M'=(\\sigma',D,\\rho',\\phi')\\\\&\\land I\\subseteq I'\\land J\\subseteq J'\\land\\alpha'\\restriction I=\\alpha\\land\\beta'\\restriction J=\\beta\\\\&\\land\\rho'\\restriction I=\\rho\\land\\phi'\\restriction J=\\phi\\end{aligned}\\right).","display":true},{"tex":"\\operatorname{InessExp}_{68}(M,\\sigma,M',\\sigma')\\;\\Longleftrightarrow\\;\\operatorname{Expansion}_{68}(M,\\sigma,M',\\sigma')\\land I'=I\\land\\forall j\\in J'\\setminus J\\;\\beta'(j)=0.","display":true}],"bytes":1965,"backlinks":[{"id":"72fcab1b1a0c4d18","anchor":"ref-3","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\operatorname{InessExp}_{68}(M,\\sigma,M',\\sigma')$，见 [[68-df-inessential-expansion]]。$\\operatorname{StrongUnd}_{68}$、$\\operatorname{Theory}_{68}$、$\\operatorname{Model}_{68}$ 与 $\\operatorname{DecTheory}_{68}$ 见 [[68-df-theory-decidability]]。"},{"id":"f850298d5e806601","anchor":"ref-84","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[68-df-inessential-expansion]]"},{"id":"be41c4d7dd143cb1","anchor":"ref-37","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[68-df-inessential-expansion]] — definition"},{"id":"3cb8c24064050ea6","anchor":"ref-84","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[68-df-inessential-expansion|df-inessential-expansion — Expansions by Constants]]"}],"outgoing":["285deaa50ea04329"]}